      "round_summary": "Repair round 2 (fix 2): target `swap.sum_preserved_under_swap`. Error category: dut_bug. Root cause: `tmp` was a register causing stale-value corruption on first swap. Fix attempt 1 (Wire only) failed to compile because a Wire assigned only inside `when(true.B)` is treated as conditionally uninitialized. Fix 2: remove the `when(true.B)` wrapper entirely — all three assignments (`tmp := x(p); x(p) := x(m); x(m) := tmp`) are now unconditional, which is correct because the swap should execute every cycle. `tmp` (Wire) gets a continuous combinational assignment from `x(p)`, and both register updates happen every cycle. The `first_cycle` guard is retained for RegNext initialization. All assertion labels preserved.",
