      "round_summary": "Repair round 3: target `swap.swap_m_gets_old_p` and `swap.swap_p_gets_old_m` (still failing after rounds 1-2). Error category: assertion_error. Root cause: Chisel's `when (!first_cycle) { fvAssert(...) }` block is silently ignored during Verilog generation — `fvAssert` produces module-level SVA properties that are unconditionally active. The `first_cycle` register exists in the hardware but the enclosing `when` block never gates the generated assertion. Fix: embed the first-cycle guard directly in each assertion expression as `fvAssert(!first_cycle || (...))` so that when `first_cycle=true` the assertion is trivially satisfied. All three RegNext-dependent assertions (`swap_p_gets_old_m`, `swap_m_gets_old_p`, `sum_preserved_under_swap`) are repaired homologously. Assertion labels preserved exactly.",
